Pl. look at schematic attached.

As shown, Linux box is between Our Private Network &
Router(which is connected to internet with leased
line).I have installed Red Hat Linux 9 with IP tables.
Static IP are assigned to outside interface card of
Linux(203.199.128.169) & Interfaces of the Cisco
Router.Private IPs are in range of 192.168.2.0.

We have used the following commands in terminal:

iptables -t nat -A POSTROUTING -s 192.168.2.0/24 \-j
SNAT -o eth1 --to-source 203.199.128.169 
OR
iptables -t nat -A POSTROUTING -o eth0 -j MASQUERADE 

iptables FORWARD -t filter -i eth1 -m state \--state
NEW,ESTABLISHED,RELATED -j ACCEPT

echo 1 > /proc/sys/net/ipv4/ip_forward

There were no errors when I executed above commands.

When I access internet through linux box, I am able to
browse but NAT is done at router. If I remove NAT
commands from router, I cannot access internet through
linux box.
Could u please let me know my mistake?


